GIVEN item IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 4 row`
`sch 4 part 2 the row for the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF item EQUALS "table 1 item 1" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 1 item 1 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 2 item 1" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 2 item 1 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 2 item 2" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 2 item 2 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 3 item 1" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 3 item 1 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 3 item 2" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 3 item 2 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 3 item 3" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 3 item 3 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 3 item 4" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 3 item 4 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 4 item 1" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 4 item 1 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 4 item 2" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 4 item 2 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 5 item 1" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 5 item 1 row`
        IF item EQUALS "table 5 item 2" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 table 5 item 2 row`
        IF item EQUALS "appellate item 1" THEN JUST `sch 4 part 2 appellate item 1 row`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Fourth Schedule has no such item in this Part

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Fourth Schedule Part 2 -- what the text says besides the tables`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `sch 4 part 2 para 1 kind of hearing` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 part 2 para 1(a) a hearing before a District Judge or a Magistrate in open court, including applications fixed on special hearing dates`
    `sch 4 part 2 para 1(b) a hearing before the Registrar in the State Courts for the examination of witnesses`
    `sch 4 part 2 para 1(c) a hearing before a Judge sitting in the General Division in open court or applications fixed in chambers or in open court on special hearing dates`
    `sch 4 part 2 para 1(d) a hearing before the Registrar in the General Division for the assessment of damages, the taking of accounts, the making of inquiries and references`
    `sch 4 part 2 para 1(e) a hearing before the Registrar in the General Division for the examination of witnesses`
    `sch 4 part 2 para 1 another hearing`

-- src:8455 | 1. The fees payable for any cause or matter for hearing — ( a )
-- src:8456 | before a District Judge or a Magistrate in open court, including applications (interlocutory or otherwise) fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates;
-- src:8457 | ( b )
-- src:8458 | before the Registrar in the State Courts for the examination of witnesses;
-- src:8459 | ( c )
-- src:8460 | before a Judge sitting in the General Division (excluding the Family Division) in open court and applications (interlocutory or otherwise) fixed for hearing in chambers or in open court on special hearing dates;
-- src:8461 | ( d )
-- src:8462 | before the Registrar in the General Division (excluding the Family Division) for the assessment of damages, the taking of accounts, the making of inquiries and references under Order 33, Rule 42; and
-- src:8463 | ( e )
-- src:8464 | before the Registrar in the General Division (excluding the Family Division) for the examination of witnesses,
-- src:8465 | are specified in the following Tables:
@ref Sch 4 part 2 para 1 (src:8455-8465)
GIVEN kind IS A `sch 4 part 2 para 1 kind of hearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 2 para 1 the Tables specify the fee for the hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 1(a) a hearing before a District Judge or a Magistrate in open court, including applications fixed on special hearing dates` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 1(b) a hearing before the Registrar in the State Courts for the examination of witnesses` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 1(c) a hearing before a Judge sitting in the General Division in open court or applications fixed in chambers or in open court on special hearing dates` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 1(d) a hearing before the Registrar in the General Division for the assessment of damages, the taking of accounts, the making of inquiries and references` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 1(e) a hearing before the Registrar in the General Division for the examination of witnesses` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 1 another hearing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 names the hearings (a) to (e) and has no "only"; the Family Division is excluded from (c), (d) and (e) in the text

-- src:8549 | 2. The following fee is payable for appeals or any other hearing before the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal:
@ref Sch 4 part 2 para 2 (src:8549)
GIVEN `the hearing is an appeal or any other hearing before the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee in the Table below is payable for the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the hearing is an appeal or any other hearing before the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appeals or any other hearing before the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal"

-- The payment details of each Table: who must pay the fees and file the Request in Form 98, and when.
-- src:8476 | The claimant, the appellant or the applicant (as the case may be) must pay the fees and file the Request, in Form 98, at the time he or she sets the cause or matter down for hearing, files the record of appeal, files his or her request for special or further hearing dates, or at the time the Registry so requires, as the case may be
@ref Sch 4 part 2 table 1 (src:8476)
GIVEN `the fees are paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Request is filed in Form 98` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was done at the time the cause or matter is set down for hearing, the record of appeal is filed, the request for special or further hearing dates is filed, or at the time the Registry so requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 2 table 1 the fees are paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` MEANS
    IF `the fees are paid` AND `the Request is filed in Form 98` AND `that was done at the time the cause or matter is set down for hearing, the record of appeal is filed, the request for special or further hearing dates is filed, or at the time the Registry so requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must pay the fees and file the Request"; the Schedule does not say what follows

