-- src:8560 | The appellant or the applicant must pay the fee and file the Request, in Form 98, within 14 days after he or she files his or her Case or at the time he or she files the application, or before the second or each subsequent day of hearing, as the case may be
@ref Sch 4 part 2 paragraph 2 payment (src:8560)
DECLARE `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the occasion` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` HAS `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the date the Case is filed` IS A DATE, `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the last day of the 14 days after the Case is filed` IS A DATE
    `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant or applicant files the application` HAS `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the date the application is filed` IS A DATE
    `sch 4 part 2 para 2 a second or subsequent day of hearing is about to begin` HAS `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the date the day of hearing begins` IS A DATE

-- "The appellant or the applicant must pay the fee and file the Request, in Form 98, within 14 days after he or she files his or her Case or at the time he or she files the application,
-- or before the second or each subsequent day of hearing, as the case may be": the occasion says which of the three times applies, and the date is when both were done.
-- The last day of the 14 days is Order 3, Rule 3's count and is given by the caller.  A bare "must" not done at all answers NOTHING (QB);
-- done, but outside the time the text fixes in its own words, JUST FALSE (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05).
@ref Sch 4 part 2 paragraph 2 payment (src:8560)
GIVEN `the fee is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Request is filed in Form 98` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date by which both were done` IS A DATE
      occasion IS A `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the occasion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 part 2 para 2 the fee is paid and the Request filed as the Schedule requires` MEANS
    IF `the fee is paid` AND `the Request is filed in Form 98`
    THEN CONSIDER occasion
         WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant files his or her Case` caseFiled lastDay THEN
             IF `the date by which both were done` AT LEAST caseFiled AND `the date by which both were done` AT MOST lastDay
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after he or she files his or her Case"
         WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 2 the appellant or applicant files the application` applicationFiled THEN
             IF `the date by which both were done` EQUALS applicationFiled
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time he or she files the application"
         WHEN `sch 4 part 2 para 2 a second or subsequent day of hearing is about to begin` dayBegins THEN
             IF `the date by which both were done` LESS THAN dayBegins
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the second or each subsequent day of hearing"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must pay the fee and file the Request"; the Schedule does not say what follows
